Below is a PowerShell script to disable the lock screen for the currently logged-in user on Windows Server 2022.

This uses the user policy registry key (HKCU), which is the correct approach when you want it per-user, not system-wide.

✅ PowerShell script (per-user)
# Disable Lock Screen for current user

$RegPath = "HKCU:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Personalization"

# Create key if it doesn't exist
if (-not (Test-Path $RegPath)) {
    New-Item -Path $RegPath -Force | Out-Null
}

# Set NoLockScreen value
New-ItemProperty `
    -Path $RegPath `
    -Name "NoLockScreen" `
    -PropertyType DWORD `
    -Value 1 `
    -Force | Out-Null

Write-Output "Lock screen disabled for current user."

🔄 Apply immediately (no reboot)
gpupdate /force


User must log out and back in for full effect.

❌ To re-enable lock screen (undo)
Remove-ItemProperty `
    -Path "HKCU:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Personalization" `
    -Name "NoLockScreen" `
    -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

⚠️ Important notes (Server 2022)

Works on Windows Server 2022 (Desktop Experience)

Applies only to the current user

Does not affect RDP session timeout / screen saver lock

If a domain GPO enforces lock screen, it will override this
